55,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Candidate C, the Supplier Data Hub, addresses the misrouted deliveries and the redundant vendor queries Ryuji mentioned.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,May,,"Candidate D, the Workflow Assistant, sounds like it helps the coordination group, but does it require too much developer time?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Candidate A, the Field Service App, mentions synchronization for records away from the network, which solves my coverage concern.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate C fits the software allowance and solves the redundant query issue without needing a massive capital investment.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Candidate B, the Training Studio, is a narrow tool for specific skills. Those are the ones that actually survive!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, but the Training Studio doesn't stop the daily time loss from copying records. Candidate C does.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, would Candidate C require the in-house developers? If so, we have to wait until Q3.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Daisuke, Candidate C is a central repository. It's safer than A if we can't guarantee plant access.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate C is likely a configuration of existing software, fitting our allowance and solving the data duplication.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I see the point, but Candidate C is a ""standardization effort."" Those usually fail without an owner.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,But the cost of doing nothing is an hour a day per person in some offices.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm leaning toward C if it doesn't break the staff rota, but D would help the coordinators.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,A is too risky given the network logs. C is the most rational choice for the company's current state.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"C addresses the budget, the vendor redundancies, and the data errors. It is the most logical.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"If we can ensure it's not a ""daily entry for everyone"" chore, I can support C.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I vote for C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,May,,"I'll go with C as well, provided it's managed centrally.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,C is my choice.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'll join the majority. C it is.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
